  "rationale": "Universities own their staff: world-step.ts phase 2a creates UNIVERSITY_STAFF link rows every tick and scribeThroughputFor reads this university staff instead of the universe whole scribe pool. The movement in this file is NOT the scribing rule. The discriminating control was run: a build that keeps assignStaff and staffingIndex, so the link entities are still allocated, and reverts ONLY scribeThroughputFor to the old global-pool loop reproduces the treatment EXACTLY, metric for metric, on all seven regressed rows and every passing row. So all of the movement is entity-handle re-allocation: contracts.md section 6 splits the RNG per entity handle, and allocating a new row shifts every handle allocated after it, which re-rolls every handle-keyed draw in the run. Corroborated by construction: the reference universe has exactly ONE university, where owning every cohort and sharing the universe pool are the same arithmetic, and a seeded 36-tick A/B at one university gives 142 books on both builds. Four of the seven rows are denial-warden alone and every regressed cell has a tolerance far narrower than the same metric family elsewhere (0.38 to 15.75 here against 20 to 120 on other strategies), which is the signature of a low-variance cell that a re-roll clears trivially. THIS FILE IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A BALANCE CLAIM: release-plan.md forbids a balance claim before 0.5.0 and nothing here is one. The universe remains degenerate in the ways the first note records.",
